WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:04.458
Python provides the type function so we can inspect
how it has classified a value

00:00:05.382 --> 00:00:09.566
In this example age is an integer height is a float
name is a string

00:00:09.816 --> 00:00:15.448
and the student flag is Boolean Run the example and
compare the result

00:00:15.474 --> 00:00:21.068
with the values that were assigned Then place
quotation marks around the age value and run

00:00:21.095 --> 00:00:26.384
it again Even though the characters still look like
the number thirty Python will now

00:00:26.397 --> 00:00:31.983
treat the value as text This distinction becomes
very important when we

00:00:31.996 --> 00:00:37.775
import data from CSV files forms or APIs A value may
look numeric

00:00:37.801 --> 00:00:40.301
to us but still arrive in Python as a string
